# Copy to .env and adjust so the app can reach your backend.
#
# - iOS simulator: http://localhost:4000 usually works.
# - Android emulator: use http://10.0.2.2:4000 (localhost on the host machine).
# - Physical phone (Expo Go): use your computer's LAN IP, e.g. http://192.168.1.23:4000
#   (phone and computer must be on the same Wi-Fi network).
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:4000

# "Google ile devam et" (see src/screens/Giri.tsx and src/utils/googleAuth.ts).
# Create OAuth client IDs at https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
# (one each for iOS, Android, and Web/Expo Go) and paste them here. The Web
# client ID is also what you should set as GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID on the backend
# (see backend/.env.example) - Google issues ID tokens addressed to it even
# when the sign-in happened through the iOS/Android client. Leave all three
# empty to keep the button showing a "not configured yet" message instead of
# a broken sign-in attempt.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID=
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_ANDROID_CLIENT_ID=
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=
